 "notes": "Curve is the upper boundary of the 'Allowed HP CDM' region in Fig. 5 (vector file HP.pdf from the e-print), i.e. the paper's own cosmological exclusion of hidden-photon cold dark matter, combining the four constraints derived in Secs. 4.1-4.2 that bound the allowed region from above: tau_2>1 (condensate survival), CMB distortions (FIRAS), N_nu^eff, and X-rays from gamma'->3gamma decay. Coordinates recovered from the PDF path of the semi-transparent pink fill; axes calibrated with the figure's major tick marks (log10 m_gamma' [eV] vs log10 chi). Boundary clipped at the plot frame (left edge log10 m=-12.38, bottom log10 chi=-16). The near-vertical step near 1e-9 eV (chi dropping from ~4e-10 to ~5e-13) is the dashed transition between the tau_2>1 and CMB-distortion regimes as drawn. Bound is cosmological (assumes gamma' is all of the DM relic) and does not depend on the local halo density, so no rho_DM rescaling applied. The paper quotes no statistical confidence level for these theory-derived bounds; 0.95 is nominal.",
